    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d335">

                <pb facs="0566" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg540"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 GE/4–2154: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé at Saigon</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McClintock</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Department of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vientiane</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-04-21T14:00:00+07:00">April 21, 1954—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>30. Sent Saigon 92, Paris 20. Paris for Ambassador Heath. In separate talks on April 15 and 17 with Crown Prince
                    and Prime Minister the following was gathered re Laotian ideas on Geneva
                    Conference.</p>
                <p>Though still vague in its thinking, Lao Government will probably follow French
                    lead but only under condition French and/or great <pb facs="0567" n="541"
                        xml:id="pg541"/> powers guarantee all Viet Minh evacuate Laos. This holds
                    true whether French desire talks re peace, truce or other negotiations.</p>
                <p>Lao Government skeptical of chances of success either Korean or Indochina phases
                    at Geneva.</p>
                <p>Prime Minister stated he and Foreign Minister ready attend preliminary
                    discussions and conference itself but are awaiting invitations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >McClintock</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
